Tab Elements
Tab Elements
The tab Elements provides a context menu with the commands for inserting dialog items into the dialog
you are creating.
Remarks
To Insert a Dialog Item into Your Dialog, click into the text box with the right mouse button and select
the respective item on the context menu.
You can also select to show or hide the Default Buttons (OK, Cancel and Apply) and to open the dialog
you create Modal, meaning that the user cannot open another dialog until he closes the present dialog.
Then the user can only open another dialog after he closed the active dialog.
Once you have inserted dialog items, the tree shows the structure of your dialog. Changing the order in
the structure modifies the layout of the dialog.
To change the order of the tabs in the dialog, select a tab on the tab Elements, hold down Shift and press
the up arrow or the down arrow to move this tab to the left or to the right. The dialog shows the first tab in
the structure as the leftmost tab.
Tab Elements
Plant Simulation Help 11-5039
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Open
To modify an existing dialog item, right-click it and select Open on the context menu. This opens the
dialog of the Dialog Item where you can change it.
Delete
To delete a dialog item, right-click it and select Delete on the context menu.
See also
Insert a Dialog Item into Your Dialog
Define Properties of a Dialog Item
Set Parameters for Objects in Your Own Dialog
Inserting a Dialog Item into Your Dialog
Insert a Dialog Item into Your Dialog
Before you start creating your dialog, take a few moments to decide about its structure, i.e., which dialog
items do you need, can you show them all in a flat hierarchy in the dialog or do you need to insert tabs and
menus.
Remarks
The structure you decide upon determines how and in which order you create the dialog items. Let us say,
you want to show the dialog items on tabs. Then, you first have to create the Tab Control, which is the
container that accommodates the individual tabs. After this you have to create the individual Tabs, and
finally you can insert the dialog items on each one of these tabs.
• To create a new dialog item, select one of these items on the context menu:
New Button New List View
New Check Box New Menu/New Menu Command
New DropDownList Box New Radio Button
New Edit Text Box New Static Text Box
New Group Box New Tab Control
New Image New Tab Page
New List Box
Inserting a Dialog Item into Your Dialog
11-5040 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To add one tab at a time to a Tab Control, click it with the right mouse button on the tab Elements,
select Tab Page on the context menu, and type in a name and caption into the text box Dialog Item Tab
Page.
• To add a dialog item to a tab on a Tab Control you created, click the name of the tab with the right
mouse button in the structure on the tab Elements and select the item you want to insert on the
context menu.
You can type in the same Name for dialog items, as long as those dialog items are not located in the same
group of items. Groups of items are: Group Box, Menu, Tab Control and Tab.
To rearrange the order of items of type Tab within a Tab Control and Menu in the structure on the tab
Elements within these groups, use Shift+Up arrow or Shift+Down arrow. The structure shows all other
dialog items according to their position in the user-defined dialog itself.
To move items out of one of the groups or place them there, click the item with the left mouse button in
the structure, drag it to the new location and drop it there.
