New Check Box
Inserts a check box into the dialog. You can also select if the check box functions as an Inheritance box.
Image on the Tab Elements
Description
A check box displays a setting or a set of settings that do not exclude each other. The user can select or
clear one or several check boxes at the same time.
Proceed as follows:
• Type in the Name of the check box.
• Type in the Caption that describes what the check box does.
• Type in the Callback Argument, which will be passed to the Callback Method as a parameter.
It will be executed, when the user selects or clears the check box.
• Type in its X and Y position in the Dialog.
• Select if you want to Enable the dialog item or not.
• Select the check box Inheritance box so that the Dialog shows the check box as a check box for
inheritance. It looks like a check box for inheritance in the dialogs of the built-in objects. The check box
also works like this.
New Check Box
Plant Simulation Help 11-5043
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Clear the check box Inheritance box so that the Dialog shows the check box as a normal check box.
Our callback method looks like this:
param action: string
switch action
case "NameEdit"
   ?.setCheckBox("NameInherit", false) 
   // clear check box when the value changes
case "Open"
   ?.setCaption("NameEdit", ?.NameValue)
   ?.setCheckBox("NameInherit", ?.NameValue.InheritValue)
case "Apply"
   var inherit:boolean := ?.getCheckBox("NameInherit") // 'inherit' is a 
user-defined variable
   if inherit
       ?.NameValue := ?.Origin.NameValue // 'NameValue' is a user-defined 
attribute
       ?.NameValue.InheritValue := true
       ?.setCaption("NameEdit", ?.NameValue)
   else
       ?.NameValue := ?.getValue("NameEdit")
       ?.NameValue.InheritValue := false
   end
end
• To insert the dialog item into your dialog, click OK.
New Check Box
11-5044 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

