It will be executed when the user changes the contents of the Text Box and selects another dialog item
afterward, clicks in another text box, or clicks OK, Apply or Cancel.
If the edit text box has a Callback Argument, the Callback Method of the Dialog will be called and the
Callback Method is assigned the callback argument _Enter, when the user presses the Enter key and if
the dialog does not show the Standard Buttons.
• Select which kind of characters the user can type into the text box.
Setting The user can type in
Any Character any character, which includes special characters, lower and upper case
letters and numbers.
Letters and Digits lower and upper case letters, including special characters, such as
umlauts, and letters of any kind of language, underscores, and blank
spaces. The user can also type in the digits 0 to 9.
Letters lower and upper case letters, including special characters, such as
umlauts, and letters of any kind of language, and blank spaces.
Decimal Number 0123456789
Signed Decimal Number decimal numbers with a negative or positive sign: -+0123456789
Hexadecimal Number ADbf09, for example.
Octal Number 01234567, but not 18 for example.
Binary Number 0 or 1
Floating Point Number 12.3E-45, for example.
