Caption [text box] - Dialog
Certain dialog items show the text box Caption. Type in the text which the Dialog shows as the caption of
the dialog item in your dialog.
Remarks
A caption is especially handy if you develop libraries in several languages and want the user to be able to
switch languages. In addition, you can type in special characters and blanks, which you cannot use in the
name.
The Caption applies to these dialog items:
New Static Text Box
New Button
New Group Box
New Check Box
New Menu/New Menu Command
New Tab Page
New Radio Button
Create an Access Key
Type in the ampersand character & in front of a letter of the Caption of the dialog items listed above
to make this letter the access key (mnemonic key). Plant Simulation activates this dialog item, when you
press Alt and that letter.
If you want to use the ampersand character & instead of and in a dialog item, for example Drag & Drop,
type in the & twice, Drag && Drop.
Caption [text box] - Dialog
Plant Simulation Help 11-5069
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
If your dialogs do not show the access keys, make sure that Settings > Ease of Access > Keyboard >
Change how keyboard shortcuts work is On.
